  "modelingNotes": [
    "IGN March 2023 returns and Roofer 1.0.0 LoD2.2 reconstruction provide semantic roof patches and the initial roof-height envelope. Missing perimeter strips are restored against the source footprint supplied to Roofer, simplified by 0.15 m. Original Roofer geometry is retained separately in baseline/.",
    "Astra replaces the planar Roofer roof approximation with a locally fitted quadratic shell using only classified roof returns within 3 m of Roofer roof surfaces. Reserved 10 m cells are excluded from the curve fit; Roofer used the full cloud, so this is held-out refinement validation, not an independent end-to-end survey.",
    "The 1991 inspected photograph supports a thin white shell and gridded structural glazing. Shell thickness 0.65 m, glazing setback 2 m and simplified frame spacing are visual inferences, not LiDAR measurements; modern doors, lettering and interiors are not reconstructed.",
    "Z=0 is the robust 62.3205 m IGN69 surrounding plaza datum. Below-plaza geometry is clipped to map ground, not a claim that the varying road/plaza terrain or hidden foundations are flat. Heights are not rescaled to the old OSM 50 m tag.",
    "Measured IGN roof and mapped plan are unchanged; only approved Clair material factors were updated."
  ],
